{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-0129"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Growing Of Other Perennial Crops Coordination"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "0129"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :agriculture/other-perennial-crop-cultivation
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:rural-livelihoods :farm-labor-efficiency :pesticide-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :perennial-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :telemetry]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :blueprint
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "`:perennial-governor` is implemented end-to-end in `src/perennial` as a
 PERENNIAL-CROP-CULTIVATION FARM OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor -- Perennial
 Advisor (LLM proposal-only) ⊣ Perennial-Crop Operations Governor (closed-
 op-allowlist / cultivation-lot-registration-before-any-action hard-gate /
 applicator-license-sprayer-calibration-pre-harvest-interval-restricted-
 entry-interval-wind-speed-buffer-zone hard-gates / unresolved-crop-
 health-flag hard-gate / field-equipment-and-pesticide-decision permanent
 block). `:itonami.blueprint/robotics` is honestly `false` -- this actor
 holds NO harvester/sprayer/applicator field-equipment-control authority
 (a HARD, permanent governor block, never overridable by human approval --
 see `perennial.governor` ns docstring). ISIC Rev.5 0129 is the RESIDUAL
 (not-elsewhere-classified) perennial-crop growing division -- perennial
 crops not already covered by 0121-0127 (grapes / tropical-subtropical
 fruits / citrus / pome-and-stone fruits / other tree-and-bush fruits and
 nuts / oleaginous fruits / beverage crops): the concrete illustrative
 crops chosen for this build are BAMBOO (culm harvest), CORK OAK (bark
 stripping), and ornamental/nursery trees and shrubs, all grown and OWNED
 by the operator (unlike ISIC 0161, support activities for crop
 production, which never owns the crop it services). Every one of its
 four proposal ops (`:log-cultivation-record` / `:schedule-field-
 operation` / `:flag-crop-health-concern` / `:order-supplies`) carries
 `:effect :propose` ONLY -- the governor HARD-holds any proposal that
 doesn't (`effect-not-propose-violations`). Crop-operation types split
 into mechanical harvest/maintenance (bamboo culm harvest, cork bark
 strip, ornamental pruning -- no chemical-application safety window at
 all) and chemical-application (herbicide/fungicide/insecticide, a
 genuine pre-harvest interval, restricted-entry interval, maximum safe
 wind speed, and minimum buffer zone) -- the Governor's chemical-specific
 checks are skipped entirely, never fabricated, for mechanical
 crop-operation types. `:flag-crop-health-concern` always escalates to a
 human, at every phase, regardless of advisor confidence;
 `:order-supplies` above a cost threshold likewise always escalates. This
 build ships NO JVM-only interop anywhere in `src/` (all source is
 `.cljc`) per this workspace's cljs-first runtime-priority rule. See
 `README.md` for the full governor-check enumeration."}
